      "body": "<!-- Thank you for your contribution! Please follow these guidelines to enhance your pull request. If anything is unclear, submit your PR and reach out to maintainers for assistance. Join our Slack community at https://slack.sglang.io to discuss further. -->\r\n\r\n<!-- PR title: [Type] scope: title, or [Type] [Hardware] scope: title.\r\nType: Feat, Fix, Refactor, Perf, Doc, Test, CI, or Chore.\r\nScope: any module or model name (no fixed list or letter-case restriction), e.g. attention, qwen3, or flash-attn.\r\nHardware: optional single tag without spaces. Use uppercase hardware tags (AMD, NVIDIA, NPU, MI300X), except for exactly these four spellings: Intel, Apple, Huawei, Ascend.\r\nTitle: no letter-case restriction.\r\nReverts: use GitHub's default title, Revert \"original title\".\r\nExamples: [Fix] attention: Fix KV cache indexing; [Perf] [AMD] flash-attn: Optimize decode performance. -->\r\n\r\nAssisted-by: OpenAI Codex\r\n\r\n## Motivation\r\n\r\nWhen a request finishes before its first Mamba tracking interval, the [int8-checkpoint path](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/6cac4dc3fe9a4bf15009f300132c3c7a1853c210/python/sglang/srt/mem_cache/unified_cache/components/mamba.py#L609-L627) reads an unwritten ping-pong state slot, then discards the zero-length checkpoint. The read is unnecessary; no output corruption was observed. Related [PR #44718](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/44718) and [PR #39209](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/39209) address different checkpoint cases.\r\n\r\n## Modifications\r\n\r\nSkip the state read when tracked length is zero.\r\nNonempty checkpoints are unchanged.\r\nNo user-facing documentation changes are needed.\r\n\r\n## Accuracy Tests\r\n\r\n- Historical Qwen3.5-0.8B-Base HTTP warmup: the unwritten-state read disappeared after the fix. [Evidence](../../new-dynamic-findings-260904.md#sg-d1-zero-length-int8-mamba-checkpoint-reads-uninitialized-state).\r\n- On main `2e7c9d851c`, the focused checkpoint suite passed `2/2` with CPU-device and `datasets` stubs. Current-main serving replay remains pending.\r\n\r\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\r\n\r\nNot measured since only the finished zero-length path changes.\r\n\r\n## Checklist\r\n\r\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\r\n- [x] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\r\n- [x] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\r\n- [x] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\r\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\r\n\r\n## Review and Merge Process\r\n\r\n1. Ping Merge Oncalls to start the process. See the [PR Merge Process](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.github/MAINTAINER.md#pull-request-merge-process).\r\n2. Get approvals from [CODEOWNERS](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.github/CODEOWNERS) and other reviewers.\r\n3. Trigger CI tests with [comments](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#how-to-trigger-ci-tests) or contact authorized users to do so.\r\n   - Common commands include `/tag-and-rerun-ci`, `/tag-run-ci-label`, `/rerun-failed-ci`\r\n4. After green CI and required approvals, ask Merge Oncalls or people with Write permission to merge the PR.\r\n\r\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\r\n---\r\n### CI States\r\n\r\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #39586826670](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39586826670)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\r\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #39586826668](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39586826668)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\r\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #39586826606](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39586826606)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\r\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
